{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c5e97f40cb7189f3","type":"group","x":-2300,"y":-1120,"width":864,"height":920,"color":"3","label":"Conceptos previos, requerimientos para el flujo y Pruebas "},
		{"id":"b99bca1e47175855","type":"text","text":">[!important]  Flujo para crear una `new PLMN` y lanzar un `PLMN launch update`","x":-1320,"y":-905,"width":580,"height":88},
		{"id":"e88e38c3709975be","type":"text","text":"***`Device`***\nRecibe el archivo binbario","x":125,"y":280,"width":216,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6195c632a7ff2a8c","type":"text","text":"***`API`*** Recibe en ***`POST /api/plmn-list/:id/launch`*** y diferencia entre `newDevice oldDevice` para enviar el `cmd`","x":-189,"y":-696,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d8766cb768cdc905","type":"text","text":"***`micro translator`*** \n***`handleOutputCommand()\n   → processCommand()`*** traduce el comando a formato device: y Publica en ***`cl.output.perte.coap.driver`***","x":306,"y":-696,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8a4fbaaacbb50884","type":"text","text":"***`mensaje`***\n```js\nMensaje: {\n     deviceInformation: { _id, serialNumber, connectivity: \"nbiot\", ... },\n     cmd_ref: \"server_command_plmns_update\",\n     cmd_value: 1\n   }\n```","x":-169,"y":-932,"width":285,"height":142,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b9140f46f8fe0438","type":"text","text":"***`formato device:`***\n```js\n{ id: [974130021], ty: \"cmd\", bid: 0, d: [[11, 1]] }\n     (registro 11 = flag PLMN update, valor 1 = \"tienes actualización pendiente\")\n```","x":164,"y":-932,"width":285,"height":142,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ea48099f0b687a57","type":"text","text":">[!tip] Se crea un ***`outPutMessage`***\n\n***`outputMsgService.storeOutput()`*** guarda para reintentos","x":631,"y":-912,"width":308,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a985761d6192b239","type":"text","text":"***`micro coap`*** \n cl-perte-coap → recibe el mensaje\n   → Busca el device en MongoDB ✓\n   → Busca manufacturedDevice ✓\n   → Busca IP del device \n   → Intenta enviar CoAP POST al device","x":751,"y":-696,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4fdaa823043ef8cb","type":"text","text":"`Admin` lanza un `plmn launch update`\n\n","x":-626,"y":-680,"width":237,"height":72,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"e0f07bd11ba5d773","type":"text","text":"***`API`*** recibe en `POST /api/plmn-list` y manda mensaje en RabbitMQ → topic: `command.plmn`","x":-162,"y":-1140,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"26c1e35dd9761327","type":"text","text":"***`micro commands/plmn`***\nRecibe el mensaje \n→ Parsea la tabla texto en líneas\n→ Genera el binario con CRC16\n→ ***Envia el .bin a la API mediante `jwt` en: files/plmn/plmn_op{X}_r{Y}_{timestamp}.bin***\n\n→ Actualiza plmnlist en MongoDB: filePath + active=true","x":299,"y":-1140,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"e923e89d21c16070","type":"text","text":"***`API`***\nRecibe el fichero ","x":754,"y":-1140,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"02003b3a5408006b","type":"text","text":"`Admin` crea un `new plmn`\n\n","x":-599,"y":-1125,"width":237,"height":72,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c2b2d37b89b54ff1","type":"text","text":">[!important] `TableRevision`\n\n**listado de códigos MCC-MNC** (Mobile Country Code + Mobile Network Code) separados por saltos de línea. Mira el ejemplo comentado en el código:\n\n```\n20205    ← KPN (Países Bajos)\n20404    ← Vodafone NL\n21401    ← Vodafone España\n22210    ← Vodafone Italia\n26201    ← Telekom Alemania\n310410   ← AT&T (USA)\n...\n```\n\nSon los operadores de red donde la SIM del device tiene **permiso de roaming**. Cada operador de telecomunicaciones (en este caso Vodafone/GDSP) proporciona esta lista.\n\nCada vez que se genera un nuevo `.bin` con una tabla PLMN actualizada, lleva un `operator` y un `release` (la revisión).\n\nEntonces:\n\n- **`operator`** = identificador del operador (ej: `1` = Vodafone)\n- **`release`** (tableRevision) = versión de esa tabla (ej: `3` = tercera revisión)\n","x":-640,"y":-1380,"width":319,"height":160},
		{"id":"d5337abea677f7ca","type":"text","text":">[!tip] Se crea un ***`outPutMessage`***\n\n***`outputMsgService.storeOutput()`*** guarda para reintentos","x":-158,"y":-1380,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f8183f889e442020","type":"text","text":">[!warning] Tener en cuenta el registro `\"id\":[]`a la hora de mokear un dispositivo!!\n\n```js\n//cambiar pv dependiendo del modelo del dispositivo\n\"id\": [config.serialNumber, 7102, 1, 26, 0], // [sn, pv, pr, psr, spec]\n\"ty\": \"sample\",\n\"li\": 1, // location_id\n\"d\": [\n```","x":-1856,"y":-430,"width":392,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"798795f48945dd95","type":"text","text":">[!warning] importante como añadir en `Device` \n>el campo `network`\n\nSin `network` en `device`  no pasara el filtro para aparecer como candidato para un ***`plmn update`*** en la ventana de ***`plmn launch update`*** del ***`admin`***","x":-1852,"y":-1070,"width":388,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"2f3ac88f4dcc98d0","type":"text","text":">[!success] Flujo para Pruebas\n>\n\n>[[AKO 44 - Flujo para Actualizar firmware - Tests.canvas]]","x":-2260,"y":-530,"width":384,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"086dcd9124d9e889","type":"text","text":">[!important] campo plmn\n>El campo `plmn` es un **array de 2 números**: `[operator, [[tableRevision]]]`.","x":-323,"y":-460,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"665d1da08bc91cb5","type":"text","text":"***`Device` *** \nenvía mensaje `sync`   para actualizar su ***`network`***","x":-736,"y":-246,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"02e7aa4ad6877dfc","type":"text","text":"campos del `mensaje`\n\n```js\n{\n  \"id\": [\"23031300000001\", 4812, 23, 1, 5],\n  \"ty\": \"sync\",\n  \"ts\": 1774451808,\n  \"bid\": 1,\n  \"hw\": [\"123456789012345\", \"8934071111111111111\", \"214071234567890\", \"BC95-G\", \"V100R100C10B657SP2\"],\n  \"plmn\": [1, 3],\n  \"d\": [[10, 2, 0, 0], [11, 5, 1, 1]]\n}\n```","x":-736,"y":-460,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a1ec65f5ca867ed7","type":"text","text":"***`micro cl-pert`***  recibe el mensaje","x":-323,"y":-246,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d3ca4b93cb4a4d65","type":"text","text":"***`micro translator`***\nSyncParser.parse() descompone el array:","x":79,"y":-246,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d0eabaf11e4ae889","type":"text","text":"***`micro commands sync.perte`***\nrecibe el mensaje parseado\n","x":473,"y":-246,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c5eaaa14987dff51","type":"text","text":"***`Device` *** \nEnvía request plmn a ***`GET /:sn/plmn`*** a la  ***`CL` ***    para actualizar su red","x":-736,"y":32,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"e1fe38365bc80aea","type":"text","text":"***`micro CL`*** \nRecive mensaje en `messageProcessor.process() → retiveAction = \"plmn\" -> processPlmn` y llama a la `API` en busca del `.bin`","x":-323,"y":32,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"eed6ebb34a8adcc7","type":"text","text":"***`API`***\nResponde enviando el fichero `.bin`","x":440,"y":89,"width":325,"height":103,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f99c5077f74c573c","type":"text","text":"***`micro CL`*** \nRecive mensaje en `messageProcessor.process() → retiveAction = \"plmn\" -> processPlmn` y llama a la `API` mediante ***`token`*** en busca del `.bin`","x":75,"y":32,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"7bcf3b01637abcf0","type":"text","text":"***`Device` *** \nRecibe el ","x":-736,"y":280,"width":317,"height":160,"color":"5"}
	],
